  "summary": "The North Liberty, Iowa City Council held a meeting on whether to remove its 12 Flock license plate reader cameras, which were installed via budget approval in 2024 without a separate contract vote. After hours of public comment uniformly opposed to the cameras, and after the police chief announced a reduction in data retention from 30 to 7 days, the council voted 4-1 to table the decision for two weeks.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The information is hard sanitized after seven days and we are committed to using the system for legitimate law enforcement purposes",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "This is about the technology, the information it collects, and the fact we are handing that information over to a private third-party company we don't have any input on.",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "They voted 4-1 to table a decision until the next City Council meeting in two weeks.",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    }
  ],
